      "title": "Діалог — A first order, no pointing",
      "intro": "Ani and Andriy sit down in a café in the city center. Notice that every item ordered changes its ending: кава becomes каву, вода becomes воду — while чай and борщ don't change at all.",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Офіціантка:",
          "text": "[Доброго|DOB-ro-ho] [дня|dnya]! [Що|Shcho] [ви|vi] [будете|BOO-deh-teh]?",
          "id": "Good afternoon! What can I get you?",
          "literal": "good day! what — you — will-be (having)?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Мені|Meh-NEE], [будь|bood'] [ласка|LAS-ka], [каву|KA-voo] [і|ee] [воду|VO-doo].",
          "id": "A coffee and a water for me, please.",
          "literal": "to-me, be — kindness, coffee (знахідний) — and — water (знахідний)."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Офіціантка:",
          "text": "[Каву|KA-voo] [з|z] [молоком|mo-lo-KOM] [чи|chi] [без|bez]?",
          "id": "Coffee with milk or without?",
          "literal": "coffee — with — milk (орудний) — or — without?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Без|Bez] [молока|mo-lo-KA], [але|A-leh] [з|z] [цукром|TSOOK-rom].",
          "id": "No milk, but with sugar.",
          "literal": "without — milk (родовий), but — with — sugar (орудний)."
