    {
      "title": "Діалог — Paying",
      "intro": "Four lines that close every visit to a café.",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Рахунок|Ra-KHOO-nok], [будь|bood'] [ласка|LAS-ka].",
          "id": "The bill, please.",
          "literal": "bill, be — kindness."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Офіціантка:",
          "text": "[Разом|RA-zom] [чи|chi] [окремо|o-KREH-mo]?",
          "id": "Together or separately?",
          "literal": "together — or — separately?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ані:",
          "text": "[Окремо|O-KREH-mo], [будь|bood'] [ласка|LAS-ka]. [Карткою|KART-ko-yoo] [можна|MOZH-na]?",
          "id": "Separately, please. Can I pay by card?",
          "literal": "separately, be — kindness. by-card — allowed?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Офіціантка:",
          "text": "[Звичайно|Zvi-CHAI-no]. [Дякую|DYA-koo-yoo], [смачного|smach-NO-ho]!",
          "id": "Of course. Thank you, enjoy!",
          "literal": "of-course. I-thank, tasty!"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "**Карткою — by card, in the орудний.** Tools always take this case: *плачу карткою* (I pay by card), *плачу готівкою* (I pay cash), *пишу ручкою* (I write with a pen).",
        "**Можна? One word, one complete question.** It means \"may I?\" and works on its own in almost any situation: pointing at an empty chair, at a door, at your card. The opposite is **не можна** (not allowed)."
      ]
    }
